<title>UK: BOE says loss of gilt role in line with intl norms.</title>
<headline>BOE says loss of gilt role in line with intl norms.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said the central bank's loss of control over the gilt market and government debt auctions to the Treasury was in line with standard international practice.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very unusual for a central bank to have that role,&quot; he told a news conference. &quot;I don't think we'll be in any kind of exceptional situation. It's more a case of reverting to the norm.&quot;</p>
<p>George denied that the Bank was angry at losing responsibility for gilts, adding: &quot;A lot of my colleagues have said &quot;about time time too.'&quot;</p>
<p>New Labour Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown announced earlier this month that the Treasury would in future take charge of debt issuance.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
